L98: More recently, inspired by work in mechanistic interpretability, several “white-box” methods have emerged. These methods hypothesize that a model’s uncertainty or confusion leaves a detectable trace within its internal computational process. The seminal work by cite70†Azaria and Mitchell [2023] showed that the model’s internal states can reveal when it is “lying”. More recently cite71†Ji et al. [2024] show that hallucination risk can be predicted by the query alone.
